    "created_at": "2025-11-24T10:35:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-11-24T10:35:37Z",
    "body": "Per https://github.com/w3c/mathml-core/issues/142 MathML will likely also get an element with the same functionality as HTML `a`.\n\nHTML also has `area` which can be a hyperlink.\n\nI think the right approach is not for HTML to mention SVG `a` and MathML `a`, but to create hooks so that SVG and MathML can easily specify that a particular element type supports the same features and has the same processing as HTML hyperlinks.\n\nHTML already has some attributes that are common among multiple HTML elements, for example https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#cors-settings-attributes and the next few subsections.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
